# Z.AI GLM-4.6V-Flash — findings by Nemotron 3.5 Super VL 120B A12B

> Source: Z.AI (glm-4.6v-flash)
> Date: 2026-10-25 (UTC)
> Overview and scoring methodology: ../../model-comparison.md
> Cross-model signed log: ../../model-findings.md

## Model card

- **Name:** GLM-4.6V-Flash
- **Short description:** Z.AI's free lightweight multimodal flash variant in the GLM-4.6V series; video/image/text/file input, text output; native multimodal tool calling.
- **Provider / access:** Z.AI API (`glm-4.6v-flash`), Hugging Face (`zai-org/GLM-4.6V-Flash`). MIT license. Listed as "Completely Free" tier.
- **Release / knowledge:** GLM-4.6V released December 2025 (per AA); newer GLM-5.3 series exists per docs.
- **IDs:** `glm-4.6v-flash` (Z.AI API slug); `zai-org/GLM-4.6V-Flash` (HF).
- **Context window:** 128K tokens (official docs for all GLM-4.6V variants including Flash).
- **Modalities:** Video + image + text + file input; text output. Native multimodal tool calling (images/videos/documents as tool parameters). Thinking mode supported.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-25):** Listed as "Completely Free" tier in official docs; GLM-4.6V family pricing $0.30 in / $0.90 out per 1M per AA (main variant, not Flash-specific).
- **Architecture:** Multimodal MoE; Flash variant parameter count not separately published (GLM-4.6V family: 108B total / 12B active per AA). License MIT.

### Raw benchmarks found

- Artificial Analysis (GLM-4.6V family): Intelligence Index **11** (estimated; #15/67 open-weights, median 8); speed 83.9 tok/s (#17/26); cost $0.30 in / $0.90 out per 1M; context 128k tokens; text+image input.
- benchgap (GLM-4.6 family, 12 measured / 46 estimated, data 2026-10-24): GPQA Diamond 81.4% estimated ±1.7 pp; LiveCodeBench v6 86.2% estimated ±2.4 pp; SWE-bench Verified 72.2% estimated ±4.4 pp; MMLU-Pro 78.4% estimated ±6.2 pp; IFEval 87.5% estimated ±2.7 pp; Vals LiveCodeBench 81.0% measured; Vals GPQA Diamond 74.5% measured; Vals MMLU-Pro 82.2% measured.
- Conflicts: benchgap/AA data is for GLM-4.6/GLM-4.6V family, not Flash-specific; Flash variant parameter count not separately published; official blog page returned empty; Flash listed as free vs AA family pricing $0.30/$0.90.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

- Tool use: **78/100.** Native multimodal tool calling (images/videos/documents as tool params) is a key differentiator; visual tool retrieval supported.
- Reasoning: **68/100.** AA Intelligence Index 11 (est) above small-model median; GPQA Diamond 81.4% estimated; Flash variant not separately benchmarked.
- Context window: **65/100.** 128K tokens; below 256K+ of newer models.
- Multimodal: **85/100.** Native video+image+text+file input — strongest multimodal coverage in this batch; visual understanding SoTA for similar parameter scale per vendor.
- Coding: **68/100.** LiveCodeBench v6 86.2% estimated; SWE-bench Verified 72.2% estimated; positioned for agentic use rather than pure coding.
- Cost efficiency: **95/100.** "Completely Free" tier per official docs; MIT license open weights; best cost efficiency in this batch.
- **Overall Score: 78/100.** Half-up mean of the five non-cost dims; best-fit recommendation: free-tier multimodal agentic workloads where native multimodal tool use and zero API cost matter; Flash-specific benchmark data limited.

